README.md
# COPYING, LICENSE.MIT and NOTICE are deliberately NOT excluded: the image
# bundles GPL-licensed spotapi alongside this AGPL-licensed code, and both
# licenses require a copy of the license text to travel with the work
# (AGPL-3.0 / GPL-3.0 section 4). This line used to read "LICENSE", which never
# matched the file anyway - it was spelled "LICENCE" until the AGPL move.
.vscode
.idea
.pytest_cache
# Local agent state, and .claude/worktrees holds a COMPLETE second copy of this
# tree - so every root-anchored rule below (Database/Data, secrets/, *.db,
# *.log) misses the copy inside it. Hence the **/ spellings that follow.
.claude/
# Anchored patterns match the whole context-relative path and a single * never
# crosses a /, so the bare spellings only ever covered the context ROOT. A
# database or key sitting one directory down - in a worktree, say - was copied
# straight into the published image.
*.db
**/*.db
**/*.log
cookies.json
cookies2.json
cookies*.json
**/cookies*.json
# The smoketest's spotapi sessions file: live sp_dc/sp_key cookies, documented
# as living beside Database/Spotify/smoketest.py. The example file is
# placeholders and the reference the smoketest's usage text points at.
session*.json
**/session*.json
!Database/Spotify/session.example.json
# Spotify export uploads: these are complete listening histories. The drop
# folder exists to hold them, so the anchored spellings below never matched the
# files that are actually there (autoImport/<user>/Streaming_History_*.json).
autoImport/
TestData/
Streaming*.json
StreamingHistory*.json
**/Streaming*.json
**/StreamingHistory*.json
**/endsong*.json
Database/Data
**/Database/Data
Database/Users
Database/__pycache__
secrets/
**/secrets/
tmp/
.tmp
tests/
docker-compose.yml
dev.py
*.ps1
# Lint-only, dev-only: the image ships no JS bundle and needs no node runtime.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
eslint.config.js
